      "id": 1,
      "text": "Granite Falls takes its name from granite boulders that splash over Gunpowder Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granite_Falls%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pioneer Andrew Baird began an iron works beside Gunpowder Creek in 1791, owning the land that became Granite Falls.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granite_Falls%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Granite Falls was officially incorporated as a town in 1899.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granite_Falls%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Burgess Chapel, the first Black Methodist Church in Granite Falls, was founded in 1936.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
